A||||6||mrfixit58||Front Sway Bar:  87 vs 88||||5||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||01-17-2001||08:23 AM||||Does anyone know if a front sway bar from a 88 will fit on an 87? The 88 bars look larger than the eariler models.<P>Thanks, <BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||william_thorniii||01-17-2001||08:59 AM||||Roy,<P>The 88 bars are different diameters from the previous years.  All bars (Coupe, Formula, GT) are the same diameter.  I will have to reference my notes at home to determine what that diameter is.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
Z||000002||mrfixit58||01-17-2001||10:31 AM||||Yes, I realize the diameters are different. The bar I saw on the junk yard 88 looked larger than my 87. My question was "will it fit on an 87"? If so, I could remove my 87 front bar and install it on the rear, then install the larger 88 bar on the front and have cheap suspension upgrade.<P>Thoughts anyone?<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000003||Will||01-17-2001||11:10 AM||||The '88 bar is larger diameter, but it also has much longer level arms. To put that bar on an early car you'd have to move the body atachment points forward several inches. Due to the box nature of the frame rail at that point this could prove difficult at best. Do you have access to just a sway bar or to the entire '88 front suspension?||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfixit58||01-17-2001||03:49 PM||||Last time I checked the bone yard, the whole susension -- less the right upper A-arm -- was still there.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Will||01-17-2001||04:18 PM||||If you want more work, check this out: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20010116-2-004275.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20010116-2-004275.html</A> <P>It's about grafting '88 suspension into an early car. You can get the missing control arm from <A HREF="http://www.kickhill.com" TARGET=_blank>www.kickhill.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfixit58||01-17-2001||06:26 PM||||Naw! Too much work. Besides, If I wanted an 88 I would have bought one. But, it's nice to know that we have some REAL talented machanics on the forum.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||7
